export const title = "Counting Setup Example (People Counting in Zone)";
export const html = "<h1>Counting Setup Example (People Counting in Zone)</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>Instructions for configuring and using the people-counting-in-zone application.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"padding:0;overflow:hidden;\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;\">\n    <div style=\"flex:1;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2b6fa8,#1c4d78);color:#fff;padding:18px;position:relative;\">\n      <div style=\"background:#1b3a7a;display:inline-block;padding:2px 10px;border-radius:4px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">STORE</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800;\">Total In Store: 87</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"flex:1;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#9fb8c8,#6f8a9c);color:#1b2a4a;padding:18px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800;\">Total In Store: 54</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n      <p>Using the people-counting-in-zone application, you can count occupancy in real time for any unit &mdash; not just a store, but a building, a specific area within a building, floor-by-floor counts, and more.</p>\n\n      <h2>Counting Principle</h2>\n      <p>The number of people within a given space is counted as follows:</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Count entries at every entrance a person can use to enter the target space.</li>\n        <li>Count exits at every exit a person can use to leave the target space.</li>\n        <li>At each data collection interval, tally and store <strong>entry count &minus; exit count</strong>.</li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h2>Counting Conditions</h2>\n      <p>To count people as accurately as possible, follow the requirements below.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n  <tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Value</th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera tilt angle</td><td>10&#176;&ndash;25&#176;</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera height</td><td>2m&ndash;5m</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera horizontal field of view</td><td>40&#176;&ndash;110&#176;</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera resolution</td><td>1280&times;720 or higher, 16:9</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera FPS</td><td>6&ndash;30</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Camera bitrate</td><td>2Mbps&ndash;10Mbps</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Minimum detectable object size</td><td>32px wide, 64px tall</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Distance between camera and object</td><td>~15m</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 620 420\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:520px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n  <text x=\"80\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5m</text>\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2m</text>\n  <path d=\"M35,40 l14,-8 M35,40 l4,15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"28\" y=\"30\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" transform=\"rotate(20 41 38)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60,45 A40,40 0 0 1 70,85\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"75\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"12\">25&#176;</text>\n  <path d=\"M60,75 A20,20 0 0 1 65,95\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"72\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"12\">10&#176;</text>\n  <rect x=\"148\" y=\"85\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" transform=\"rotate(20 161 93)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"41\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"270\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"161\" y1=\"93\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"270\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"500\" cy=\"270\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#f2c14e\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"500\" cy=\"258\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#333\"/>\n  <line x1=\"500\" y1=\"284\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"230\" width=\"16\" height=\"90\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"345\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-start=\"url(#a5)\" marker-end=\"url(#a5)\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">~15m</text>\n\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"380\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"490\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"380\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#333\"/>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"490\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"490\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-start=\"url(#a5)\" marker-end=\"url(#a5)\"/>\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">~15m</text>\n  <path d=\"M100,570 A80,40 0 0 1 260,570\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"555\" font-size=\"12\">110&#176;</text>\n  <rect x=\"145\" y=\"575\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"a5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" refX=\"3\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Camera installation requirements: tilt angle, height, distance, field of view</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n      <ul class=\"steps\">\n        <li>Follow the entrance/exit camera installation requirements.</li>\n        <li>No one should enter or leave the target space except through the designated entrances and exits.</li>\n        <li>Set a daily counter reset time during a time window when the target space is empty of people.</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>AI Bridge Counter Setup</h2>\n      <p>To configure people counting in a zone, access the AI Bridge and click <strong>Explore AI Apps &ndash; Occupancy Counting</strong> in the sidebar navigation.</p>\n      <p>Click the button at the top right of the people-counting-in-zone list to configure a new counter.</p>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:150px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add Counter</span></div>\n      <p>Set the counter's name under <strong>Name</strong>. If you'll be integrating with a cloud server, it's a good idea to use a name you can later distinguish, since the counter name is used to identify auto-registered counters and connect them to a store.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\"><div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:70px 1fr;\"><span>Name</span><input value=\"In-Store People Count\" disabled></div>\n</div></div>\n\n      <p>Configure a counting zone for each of Entry Count and Exit Count. If there are multiple entrances or exits, you need to add a counting zone for every one of them.</p>\n\n      <h2>Counting Zone Setup</h2>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;\">\n    <div style=\"flex:1;\">\n      <div style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\">Entry Count</div>\n      <table class=\"app-table\"><tr><th>Video</th><th>Zone Name</th><th>Actions</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;color:var(--text-muted);\">+ Add</td></tr></table>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"flex:1;\">\n      <div style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\">Exit Count</div>\n      <table class=\"app-table\"><tr><th>Video</th><th>Zone Name</th><th>Actions</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;color:var(--text-muted);\">+ Add</td></tr></table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <p>Use the video selection dropdown at the top right to choose the video you want to count on.</p>\n      <p>Please refer to the video to set the counting zone appropriately. The counting zone can be configured using the features below.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Counting Zone <span>&times;</span></div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div style=\"text-align:right;margin-bottom:8px;\"><select disabled style=\"outline:2px solid #d64545;\"><option>Select Video</option></select></div>\n    <div style=\"height:200px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#4a5568,#2d3748);border-radius:6px;\">\n      <svg width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 200\"><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#f0dc3c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"150\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#f0dc3c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"420\" cy=\"60\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#f0dc3c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Setting the counting line / area on the reference video</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n      <ol>\n        <li>Dragging a vertex <strong>moves</strong> that vertex.</li>\n        <li>Clicking the yellow line of the counting line <strong>adds</strong> a new vertex.</li>\n        <li>Right-clicking a vertex <strong>deletes</strong> it.</li>\n        <li>Drag the transparent gray rectangle to set the <strong>label position</strong>.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p>Once you finish configuring the counting zone, click the button to save the settings. You'll see a new item created in the counter list.</p>\n      <p>Follow the same steps to configure entry and exit counting at every entrance and exit.</p>\n\n      <h2>Reset Schedule Settings</h2>\n      <p>You can reset the counter during a period when the target space is empty of people, such as at night or outside business hours.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:10px;\"><strong style=\"font-size:13px;\">Reset Schedule</strong> <span class=\"btn small\">+ Add</span></div>\n  <table class=\"app-table\"><tr><th>Type</th><th>Time</th><th>Actions</th></tr><tr><td>Daily</td><td>00:00</td><td>&#8942;</td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <p>Reset schedules can be configured as daily, weekly, or monthly. You can also add multiple reset schedules.</p>\n\n      <h2>Finishing Setup</h2>\n      <p>Once you've finished configuring the entry counter, exit counter, and reset schedule, click the button at the bottom to submit the people-counting-in-zone counter settings.</p>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:140px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">Submit</span></div>\n      <p>If the settings were applied successfully, you can see the configured item in the people-counting-in-zone list.</p>\n\n      <h2>Real-Time Report Settings (Optional)</h2>\n      <p>This feature sends count values in real time to an HTTP server that you configure. Not configuring this has no effect on how the counter works.</p>\n      <p>Click the Set button to configure the real-time count reporting feature.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Enable</span><span style=\"background:#2653d6;border-radius:10px;width:34px;height:18px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"><span style=\"position:absolute;right:2px;top:2px;width:14px;height:14px;background:#fff;border-radius:50%;\"></span></span>\n    <span>Report Interval</span><select disabled><option>Every 1 minute</option></select>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"section-label\">Data Recipient Server</div>\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Server URL</span><input value=\"https://\" disabled>\n    <span>Authentication</span><select disabled><option>None</option><option>Basic</option><option>Digest</option><option>Token</option></select>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"text-align:right;margin-top:10px;\"><span class=\"btn small\">Test</span></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <p>To use real-time reporting, turn on the Enable switch.</p>\n      <p>Set the real-time report interval under Report Interval.</p>\n      <h2>Data Recipient Server</h2>\n      <p>Configure information for the server that will receive real-time count data.</p>\n      <p>Provide the HTTP or HTTPS server URL, and add authentication settings if applicable. Supported authentication types are Basic, Digest, and Token.</p>\n      <p>Once you've configured the data recipient server, use the Test button to check whether the device can successfully send data to the server. Clicking Test sends data in the same format as the counter's actual real-time count data to your configured HTTP server.</p>\n      <h2>Data Transmission Format</h2>\n      <p>Under Data Transmission Format, click the expand button next to Format View to see the real-time count data transmission protocol details.</p>";
